    "title": "WHO urges 50% price hike on tobacco and alcohol by 2035 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The World Health Organization (WHO) is campaigning for significantly higher taxes on tobacco products, alcohol and sugary drinks. It is urging countries to raise the prices of these harmful products by at least 50% by 2035 through taxes. According to the UN health agency, the revenue could be used to fund the fight against heart disease, cancer and diabetes. These and other non-communicable diseases account for three-quarters of all causes of death worldwide. Citing a 2024 report by the Healthcare Tax Policy working group, which is sponsored by the non-profit Bloomberg Philanthropies, the WHO said that a one-time 50% price increase by 2035 could prevent up to 50 million premature deaths over the next 50 years. The WHO's 3 by 35 Initiative hopes to raise 1 trillion dollars over the next 10 years to invest in healthcare, education and social protection measures, the global health organization calculates. \"The 3 by 35 Initiative aims to revitalize health taxes as a powerful tool to reduce harmful consumption, save lives, and generate vital public revenue,\" the WHO said in a statement.",
